// @name: Synth euclidean rhythm
// @tagline: `play(euclid(8 5))` + a sine-LFO'd pitch — no samples
// @description: A synth voice gated by an euclidean rhythm generator (`euclid(pulses steps)` fed
//   into `play()`), pitch modulated by `sine()`. Verbatim pattern from the official mercury-lang
//   grammar test corpus (`test-grammar.txt`), which is the canonical reference for rhythmic
//   pattern functions in the language. Still synth-only — no sample-set dependency.
// @language: mercury
// @outputs: audio
// @level: intermediate
// @tags: mercury, ab-corpus, synth, euclid, rhythm, no-samples
// source: https://github.com/tmhglnd/mercury-lang/blob/main/test/test-grammar.txt
//
// A/B — mercury — Synth euclidean rhythm. Original: https://github.com/tmhglnd/mercury-lang/blob/main/test/test-grammar.txt
// Coller/évaluer la voix, puis comparer au rendu de l'outil original (mercury.timohoogland.com).
// Test de robustesse : rythmique euclidienne (`euclid`/`play`) — DOIT sonner sans samples.

core
tempo:120

actor v  eval.mercury

-----
S -> v_r

v_r -> v.`new synth square note(sine(8 5.512 0 12)) play(euclid(8 5)) time(1/16)`:4
